# Process: pick the rule before the change

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L0 router.

## Use This When

- Any implementation, refactor, schema change or investigation is about to start.
- You need to know which project rule or vendor skill owns the area you are touching.

## Stop Here If

- You have picked the narrowest rule or skill below; read that one and leave the others out of context.

## Descend To

- New artifact of any kind (component, helper, type, contract): `reuse-first-discovery.mdc` first, always.
- Where a change belongs (domain, application, presentation, adapters): `domain-context-first-analysis.mdc`.
- Data contracts and validation at boundaries: `zod-schema-first-contracts.mdc`.
- Untyped values, casts, `any`-typed library results: `no-any.mdc`.
- User-visible text: `ui-i18n-direct-keys.mdc`.
- UI controls and styling: `ui-primitive-hygiene.mdc`, then the vendor skill `.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md`.
- Anchors (data-testid), codes, the contract folder or the UI manifest: `ui-contract.mdc`, then the skill `.agents/skills/adding-ui-anchors/SKILL.md`.
- Imports that load code lazily: `static-imports-only.mdc`.
- New environment variables: `monorepo-env-minimalism.mdc`.
- Compatibility switches, legacy paths, migrations: `poc-no-fallbacks.mdc`, `reset-mode-default.mdc`.
- File and folder names, a file turning into a folder of parts, a new gateway module: `entity-first-module-naming.mdc`.
- A new package or feature module, or a change to a package's role, exports or scripts, or to a module's routes, shapes, commands or providers: `package-readme.mdc`.
- A source file at or past 300 lines, or a failing size gate: `file-size-tiers.mdc`.
- A new class, a new domain or application function, or a one-unit lint error: `one-unit-per-file.mdc`.
- Before any commit: `security-review-before-commit.mdc`.
- SurrealQL, schema and SurrealKit: vendor skills `.agents/skills/surrealql/`, `.agents/skills/surrealkit/`, `.agents/skills/surrealdb-js/`.

## Core rule

- Reads and writes of the database are declared only in `*.surql` files next to the component that owns them. TypeScript never carries SurrealQL text; it imports the compiled shape or command generated by `bun run model`.
- `bun run check` is the gate. A change is done when it is green and the output has been read.
